# The first start offers Mission Planner's settings, and Import settings brings them across, once.
#
# This application keeps its files under MissionPlannerRust, not the C#'s "Mission Planner"
# (PLAN.md section 12, D11; section 13.6 row 77), and takes nothing of Mission Planner's unasked
# (the owner, 2026-10-14: the silent import every first start made is gone). Its first start - no
# config.xml of its own - with Mission Planner's data folder there makes the offer
# (crates/mp-gui/src/mp_import.rs, the PLUGINS tab's Import from Mission Planner). Import settings
# lays Mission Planner's config.xml over this application's and copies its other artefacts by name
# - poi.txt, History and the rest - where this application has none
# (mp_settings::migrate::import_settings); the C#'s copies are left as they were. The fact
# config.imported is what this start imported, or none.
#
# Self-contained: XDG_DATA_HOME puts both applications' directories in the scratch one - the C#'s
# as "$WORK/Mission Planner", seeded below, and this application's as "$WORK/MissionPlannerRust",
# which does not exist until the start makes it. (Where a ~/Mission Planner directory exists, the
# C#'s rules put that application's directory there instead, XDG_DATA_HOME does not move it, and
# this fails. A ~/MissionPlannerRust changes nothing: PLAN.md section 12, D11.)

env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
setup mkdir -p "$WORK/Mission Planner/History" && printf '\357\273\277<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>\n<Config>\n  <distunits>Feet</distunits>\n  <MapType>OpenStreetMap</MapType>\n</Config>' > "$WORK/Mission Planner/config.xml" && printf '%s\t%s\t%s\r\n' -35.3625 149.1655 gate -35.3640 149.1640 mast > "$WORK/Mission Planner/poi.txt" && printf 'fw' > "$WORK/Mission Planner/History/firmware.hex"

tiles offline
screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 5

# Offered, and taken: what came across is read at once from where it was copied to.
expect mpimport.offer shown
click mpimport-settings
expect config.imported config.xml, poi.txt, History
expect config.distunits Feet
expect config.MapType OpenStreetMap
expect fly.poi.count 2
expect fly.poi.file ~ MissionPlannerRust/poi.txt
click mpimport-close
expect mpimport.offer none

# The second start: the offer was answered, so it is not made again and nothing is imported; what
# the first one brought is what it reads.
restart
expect mpimport.offer none
expect mpimport.answer done
expect config.imported none
expect config.distunits Feet
expect fly.poi.count 2
